# ============================================================
# artifacts/ is a Windows junction to D:\backup-manifests\2026-11-06\artifacts
# (archived 2026-11-06). Git on Windows traverses junctions, so without this
# rule `git add -A` would re-import ~2.69 GiB / 3122 archived files.
# Historical audit scripts still resolve old artifacts/... paths through the
# junction; ignoring only affects version control, not filesystem access.
# ============================================================
/artifacts/
